    <div class="km-section-header">
      <span class="km-eyebrow">OUR HERITAGE</span>
      <h1 class="km-heading-1">Handcrafted for Generations</h1>
      <p class="km-body-lead">The journey of KraftMart from metal finishing roots in 1996 to worldwide Indian heritage craftsmanship.</p>
    </div>

    <div style="line-height: 1.8; color: var(--km-text-primary); font-size: 1.05rem;">
      <h3 class="km-heading-2" style="margin: 36px 0 16px 0;">1996: Lakshmi Engineering Works</h3>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
        KraftMart was born out of Lakshmi Engineering Works, founded in Amritsar, Punjab in 1996. Specializing in high-precision nickel and chrome electroplating, machinery parts polishing, vintage vehicle accessories, and metal refining, our artisans developed decades of hands-on expertise in metal finishing.
      </p>

      <h3 class="km-heading-2" style="margin: 36px 0 16px 0;">The Transition to Heritage Craft</h3>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
        Building upon our deep metalworking legacy, we expanded into handforging traditional Sikh Kirpans, Punjabi Khandas, and ornate Rajput wedding talwars. Recognizing the demand among diaspora families and weapon collectors across the USA, Canada, UK, and Europe, KraftMart launched to bring authentic Amritsar artistry directly to customers worldwide.
      </p>

      <h3 class="km-heading-2" style="margin: 36px 0 16px 0;">Personalization & Uncompromising Quality</h3>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 20px;">
        Every ceremonial sword created by KraftMart is individually inspected, hand-polished, and fitted with premium velvet-covered scabbards and brass hilts. We offer free custom laser engraving on all orders, ensuring every piece becomes a cherished heirloom.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
